    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0453" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg441"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.61/781: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-02T21:00:00-05:00">January 2, 1941—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. We have read your telegram No. 1781 of December 26, 8 p.m. with interest and
                    fully approve the attitude taken by you during the conversation. The matter of
                    the Baltic gold, ships, Legations and so forth will be made the subject of a
                    subsequent telegram to you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
